%9Syntax:%9

    $nickmode

%9Description:%9

    $nickmode in a message format is the sender's mode prefix, coloured by
    nick_mode_color_*: ~ or & for an owner, @ for an op, %% for a halfop and
    + for a voice.

    A nick without a mode gives one space (coloured by nick_mode_color_normal),
    whatever show_nickmode_empty says, so the nick column keeps its width.
    $nickmode is empty only outside message formats.

%9Examples:%9

    pubmsgnick = "{msgnick $nickmode$nickcolored}";

    (a line of the shellter theme, in the formats section)

%9See also:%9

    FORMAT, NICK_MODE_COLOR
